.TH ROBOTS public.SH NAMErobots \- an action packed (edge of your toilet seat) game.SH SYNOPSISrobots [ -m ] [ -s ].SH DESCRIPTIONRobots is a display oriented game that requires hand, feet and eye coordination ??  This is a game I used to play on a dual unix-like machine until they took it away.  So out of addiction,robots system V was born.  The curses(3x) screen managementlibrary is used to handle the display so you must set your TERMenvironment variable.The idea is to avoid the moving robots by either running awayfrom the little buggers or by hiding behind the junk heeps thatare created when two or more robots run into each other.There are two modes of operation (Automatic and Manual mode).The automatic mode (which is the default) is for those who havethe need ... for speed  (recommended only at 9600 baud)..SS OPTIONS.P-m      manual mode.  This is more of a strategy game.          Recommended operation for bods lower than 9600..P-s      will print to stdout the log file containing the        top one hundred scores..SH SCORINGYou get points when a robot gets turned into a junk heep.Screen one starts out with twenty robots and each screenafter that is incremented by twenty robots.  Also the valueof each robot is incremented with each screen.  Your scorewill start blinking when you have made the Top Ten list andturn to reverse video when you make top gun..SH FILES/usr/games/lib/robots.log      automatic mode score sheet/usr/games/lib/robot.log       manual mode score sheet/usr/games/lib/robots.debug    debug stats .SH AUTHORPaul J. Condie .SH COMPLAINT/SUGGESTION BOX{ihnp4,lll-crg,qantel,pyramid}!ptsfa!pjc.SH BUGSNone known.